        "answer": "Catenation is the unique ability of carbon atoms to bond with each other, forming long, branched and cyclic structures. This is possible because each carbon atom can form four covalent bonds (tetravalency). The four valencies allow carbon to link to other carbon atoms as well as to various heteroatoms (H, O, N, S, halogens). The C\u2013C bonds are strong, ensuring stability of large molecules. Together, catenation and tetravalency give rise to millions of organic compounds with diverse structures and properties, far exceeding those of other elements.",
